      "title": "DaVita Stock Gains 55.6% Year to Date: What's Behind the Rally?",
      "summary": "DaVita (DVA) shares have gained 55.6% year-to-date, outpacing industry growth, driven by better operating execution, improved treatment-volume outlook, and growing confidence in value-based kidney care. The company reaffirmed 2026 guidance with expected earnings growth of 50.6% on 3.2% sales growth, supported by higher revenue per treatment and labor productivity gains. However, risks include insurance-mix headwinds from ACA subsidy losses, rising patient-care costs, and uncertain Medicare reimbursement policies.",
